From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vates Git Importer <gitimporter@vates.tech>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2015 07:09:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nfs_access_get_cached may call __nfs_revalidate_inode() which
 makes network calls and will timeout if the NFS server is unreachable.
 Currently, the error is ignored and it calls ->access() which will again make
 network calls and time out. The result is that the operation fails after
 twice the configured timeout. This can be reproduced by stat()ing a file
 within the root of the NFS mount when the NFS server is unavailable.

Fix it by handling most errors from nfs_access_get_cached().
Signed-off-by: Ross Lagerwall <ross.lagerwall@citrix.com>
---
 fs/nfs/dir.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/nfs/dir.c b/fs/nfs/dir.c
index ff030bd03717..c0f17d1f004b 100644
--- a/fs/nfs/dir.c
+++ b/fs/nfs/dir.c
@@ -2586,6 +2586,8 @@ static int nfs_do_access(struct inode *inode, struct rpc_cred *cred, int mask)
 		status = nfs_access_get_cached(inode, cred, &cache, may_block);
 	if (status == 0)
 		goto out_cached;
+	else if (!(status == -ENOENT || status == -ECHILD))
+		goto out;
 
 	status = -ECHILD;
 	if (!may_block)
